### star-metd-summarize/SKILL.md
--- 1
Do not partition by document target: a leaf commonly feeds several documents, so the file lists would overlap and the same plan be read three or four times, and conventions §6.2 gives concurrent delegates disjoint file ownership without exception. Deciding which leaf feeds which document is itself the reading this step delegates (`extract_map.md` settles it from a leaf's §2 inputs, §3 steps and §4 deliverables, never from the title), and Step 1 opens no plan body, so no exact per-document file list exists before the collectors run.
